---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Doan Van Tai" description="Doan Van Tai’s research journey from building an SDN network digital twin to studying routing decision quality under imperfect information.">
  <div class="container page-header"><a class="breadcrumb" href="/">← Home</a><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT ME</p><h1>Computer networks,<br />models, and decisions.</h1></div>
  <div class="container page-body about-page-grid">
    <article class="prose">
      <p>{profile.bio}</p>
      <p>My Vietnamese name is <strong>Đoàn Văn Tài</strong>. I’m based in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam, and expect to complete my Bachelor of Engineering in Computer Networks and Communications in 2027.</p>

      <h2>My Research Journey</h2>
      <p>My work on <a href="/work/network-digital-twin/">DT4N</a> started with a systems problem: how can a network be observed and controlled through a digital representation? I built an SDN testbed connected to Eclipse Ditto, with telemetry synchronization, anomaly detection, what-if analysis, and a closed control loop.</p>
      <p>This connects to a decision problem. A twin works with observations collected at particular times and a model of how the network will respond to an action. To understand the decisions made from that information, we need to examine both what the controller observes and what its model predicts.</p>
      <p>My ongoing <a href="/work/state-model-regret/">State–Model–Regret research</a> studies how these two factors separately and jointly affect expected routing decision regret. I use controlled queueing models and simulation to investigate the question. The work remains exploratory, with its assumptions and unresolved questions documented alongside the results.</p>

      <h2>What I’m working toward</h2>
      <p>I want to develop as a Research Engineer who can connect theoretical reasoning, simulation, experimental evidence, and working systems. My longer-term interests include graduate research in computer networks, Network Digital Twins, and AI / ML for networking.</p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>I keep model assumptions, configurations, and measurement scripts with the code. I compare results with a defined reference and document failed targets alongside successful runs.</p>
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <p><strong>University of Information Technology, VNU-HCM</strong><br/>B.Eng. Computer Networks and Communications<br/>2023–2027 (expected) · GPA 3.52 / 4.00</p>
      <h2>Technical toolkit</h2>
      <div class="skills-grid">{profile.skills.map(skill=><div class="skill-group"><h3>{skill.title}</h3><p>{skill.items}</p></div>)}</div>
      <h2>Let’s connect</h2>
      <p>I’m open to Research Intern, Research Assistant, and R&D opportunities, especially where networking, digital twins, and machine learning meet.</p>
      <p><a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> · <a href={profile.github}>GitHub</a></p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/cv/">View my CV <Icon size={15}/></a>
    </article>
    <figure class="about-page-photo"><img src="/images/tai-sunset.jpg" alt="Doan Van Tai at the seaside beneath a pink sunset" width="1368" height="1824"/><figcaption>At the seaside.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
